{"schema": 2, "id": "religion-inti", "title": "Inti", "label": "Inti", "description": "manifestation inca/panandine du soleil", "extract": "Inti est la manifestation inca/panandine du soleil. C'est une force divine reconnue par tous les peuples andins. Son origine n'est pas connue de manière certaine : selon certains, il pourrait avoir été un totem d'origine Quechua ou bien celui d'un dieu d'une autre tribu. Il est représenté par un disque solaire à face humaine et entouré de rayons lumineux.", "type": "religion", "typeLabel": "Religion", "continents": ["Ameriques"], "epochs": ["antiquite", "moyen-age", "moderne"], "from": 1, "to": 1730, "itemCount": 40, "items": ["Acre State", "Arequipa", "Ayaviri", "Cajamarca", "Calama", "Camana", "Canelos", "Caqueta", "Caracara", "Cauca", "Chachapoyas", "Chanchan", "Charcas", "Chichas", "Cuzco", "Esmeraldas", "Huamanga", "Huancavelica", "Macaya", "Maynas", "Moyobamba", "Nazca", "Oruro", "Pisqupampa", "Piwra", "Popayan", "Potosi", "Puno", "Quero", "Quijos", "Quito", "Santa Ana", "Santa Cruz de la Sierra", "Sucre", "Tarija", "Tiahuanaco", "Tucume", "Tumbes", "Ucayali", "Wankapampa"], "source": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inti", "articleLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "image": "", "imageCredit": {"filename": "Sol_de_Mayo-Bandera_de_Argentina.svg", "artist": "Juan Martín de Pueyrredón (1777-1850) , according to Ministerio del Interior website", "license": "Public domain", "licenseUrl": "", "credit": "Taken from the National flag of Argentina", "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sol_de_Mayo-Bandera_de_Argentina.svg"}, "revision": "", "sha256": "cc728977ce1a1c5de13b80f659576f40b42745213177702e6747905f5742da3e"}